some points from my experience.

I am in csh, so to set the env variable do 
setenv JULIA_CUDA_MEMORY_POOL none

] doit etre tapé, c'est pas ok un copier/coller !!

julia --project=. 


pour lancer mon .jl de test en interactif : julia --project ocean_hydro_only_test.jl test true


run in interactive mode : 
with gpu

qsub -I -q gpuq -l walltime=00:30:00


with mpi 
qsub -I -q mpi_1 -l select=1:ncpus=28:mpiprocs=28:mem=120g -l walltime=12:00:00


This has been fixed in the latest versions of Oceananigans > 108.0
I needed to change the file /data/hpcdata/users/josnez/julia/packages/Oceananigans/j2tCL/ext/OceananigansNCDatasetsExt/netcdf_writer.jl by adding the line:

default_output_attributes(model) = Dict{String, Any}()

and comment the definition:

#function default_output_attributes(model)
#    velocity_attrs = default_velocity_attributes(model.grid)
#    buoyancy = model isa ShallowWaterModel ? nothing : model.buoyancy
#    tracer_attrs = default_tracer_attributes(buoyancy)
